.TH PROOFIX 1 "September 2026" "proofix 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
proofix \- fix typos and punctuation in Markdown, under audit
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B proofix
.I input.md
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B proofix
corrects typos and punctuation in a Markdown file. Every change is one
bounded, logged, reasoned edit; the model never rewrites prose. Run it
after
.BR stylefix (1)
and before
.BR mdmemo (1).
.PP
Four tiers:
.TP
.B mechanical
A space before a comma or period, a missing space after one, doubled
punctuation, doubled words, known misspellings. Found by LanguageTool's
single-answer rules and the typos tool; applied outright.
.TP
.B adjudicated
Unknown words and grammar rules with candidate fixes. LanguageTool
proposes; a local model picks one or KEEP from the sentence and the rule's
message.
.TP
.B consistency
The same term written two ways in one document ("third-party" and "third
party"; "Frontier AI" and "frontier AI"). Families are found
deterministically; the minority occurrences are put to the model with the
rule that a compound modifier before a noun is hyphenated and a noun
phrase is open, so "a third party" survives and "third party assessors"
does not.
.TP
.B commas
Comma placement, which no rule engine detects. The model returns the
sentence with commas corrected; a diff guard admits only insertions and
deletions of commas and rejects anything else. Comma splices and other
faults the model notices are reported as notes, not changed. Serial
commas are left to stylefix's style guide.
.PP
Code, link targets, URLs, HTML and front matter are never touched.
LanguageTool runs twice: mechanical fixes first, then judgement calls on
the cleaned text.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-o ", " \-\-output " FILE"
Default: the input name with .proofed before the extension.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-in\-place
Overwrite the input.
.TP
.BR \-\-target " {us|uk}"
Variety the document is written in. Default us.
.TP
.BI \-\-accept " FILE"
Extra words never flagged as misspelled. ~/.config/proofix/accept.txt and
stylefix's accept lists are also honoured.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-lt
Skip LanguageTool (the first two tiers).
.TP
.BR \-\-lt\-level " {default|picky}"
LanguageTool rule level.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-typos
Skip the typos pre-pass.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-consistency
Skip the consistency tier.
.TP
.BR \-\-commas " {gated|all|none}"
Which sentences the comma tier sends to the model. gated (default): those
with a comma, an introductory opener, a clause trigger, or clauses joined
by a conjunction. all: every sentence. none: skip the tier.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-sentences " N"
Cap on sentences sent to the comma tier.
.TP
.BR \-\-optional\-commas " {leave|add}"
Commas that are optional by convention: leave as written (default) or
add.
.TP
.BR \-\-llm " {auto|dgx|ollama|none}" ", " \-\-url ", " \-\-model ", " \-\-timeout
Model endpoint, as in stylefix. With none, tiers two and three are
reported, not applied.
.TP
.BI \-\-min\-confidence " X"
Decisions below this are not applied. Default 0.8.
.TP
.BI \-\-parallel " N"
Concurrent model requests. Default 4.
.TP
.BI \-\-cache " FILE" ", " \-\-no\-cache
Decision cache, default .proofix/cache.json (commas in commas.json next to it).
.TP
.BI \-\-report " FILE" ", " \-\-no\-report
Markdown report, default <output>.report.md.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print a diff, write nothing.
.TP
.B \-\-changes
Print every change to standard error as it is made.
.SH PERFORMANCE
On a 20-page document (8,000 words) with a local 27B model and 8 parallel
requests: LanguageTool 4.5 s per pass; the comma tier 19 s for the 260
sentences that pass the gate; about a minute in all. Linear in length.
Decisions are cached by sentence.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR stylefix (1),
.BR mdmemo (1),
.BR languagetool (1),
.BR typos (1).
